      "lines": [
        "This pan is so hot that water stops behaving like water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "compare",
      "pad_before": 0.1,
      "pad_after": 0.2,
      "min_duration": 5.0,
      "lines": [
        "On a cooler surface, a drop spreads and evaporates. But on a very hot one, something strange happens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reveal",
      "pad_before": 0.3,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "min_duration": 5.0,
      "lines": [
        "The bottom of the drop vaporizes almost instantly, creating a thin layer of steam."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "glide",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "min_duration": 6.0,
      "lines": [
        "That vapor partly separates the water from the metal, so the drop glides instead of spreading across the surface."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "name",
      "pad_before": 0.25,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "min_duration": 6.5,
      "lines": [
        "That's the Leidenfrost effect. The drop is still evaporating, but it lasts far longer than you'd expect."
      ]
    },
